in an even-PVI district, and raters plus markets lean clearly toward Rutinel despite Evans's incumbency and cash advantage. The lone poll showing a narrow Evans lead keeps this short of Likely D.", "watch": "Fresh independent polls and the heavy outside spending on both sides could shift this back toward a true tossup if Evans keeps the race tied.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Gabe Evans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Colorado's 8th District is an even partisan split, and first-term Republican Gabe Evans faces a strong challenge from Democrat Manny Rutinel in what looks like a difficult national environment for the GOP. Evans holds a large cash-on-hand edge, but Rutinel has raised heavily and benefits from far more outside support. Expert ratings split between Tossup and Lean/Likely D, and prediction markets price Rutinel near 80% to win. The only public poll, Republican-sponsored, shows Evans narrowly ahead, and headlines describe the race as essentially tied. The forecast lands on a modest Democratic edge with wide uncertainty, reflecting the conflict between a tied race on the ground and a strongly favorable Democratic backdrop.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7882, "margin": 4.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7652, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7649, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7806, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7027, "margin": 4.0}]}